  "notes": "The trio that took progressive house mainstream, documented as \"a pulsating, progressive take on house music\" combining four-on-the-floor beats with anthemic melodic elements. The arrangement is the identity and the entry states it: \"a single sustained anthem lead is the hook, stated in the breakdown on piano or pad and then detonated at the drop\", with builds that \"can last up to four minutes\" and layers added and subtracted across 4-, 8- and 16-bar phrases. That is a 32-bar bridge, 16-bar sections throughout and the highest drop-out probability among the progressive-house models here. The melody is therefore low-density, legato and arch-weighted over 8- and 16-bar phrases, and the countermelody is the piano statement of the same line. The bass is \"a sidechained saw or pluck bass locked to the kick, with the sub dropping out entirely under breakdowns to maximise the drop's impact\" — a kick mirror at a high root probability. ⚠ The research marks the harmony `[LOW-CONF]` and says the tempo and drum grammar come from the sub-genre convention; both marks are repeated here. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the velocity tiers, the perc lanes and densities, the roll settings and every register.",
